  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing Vulnerabilities Leading to Onward Movement among Vulnerable Migrants in Eastern Sudan - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project aims to reduce vulnerabilities and adverse drivers leading to onward movement by strengthening resilience of migrants in eastern Sudan by contributing towards the following three project outcomes: (1) The MRRC Khartoum, MRCs in Gedaref and Kassala, and their referral partners further improve the protection environment for vulnerable migrants in the target states by expanding existing coordination mechanisms; (2) The resilience among vulnerable migrants and host communities in the target states is enhanced, most notably through the improved access to critical services and social cohesion initiatives; and (3) Vulnerable Ethiopian migrants in Gedaref and Kassala have continued and consistent access to protection and other assistance, as well as support for safe and dignified return and sustainable solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
